---
// Math Guides & Comparisons Component
---

<section class="guides-section" id="guides-section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-badge">
      <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"></path>
        <path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"></path>
      </svg>
      <span>Guides, Formulas & Comparisons</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Formulas, Trigonometric &theta; Table & Guides</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle">Deep dive into calculation rules, standard theta angle values, and scientific methods</p>
  </div>

  <div class="guides-grid">
    <!-- Card 0: Trigonometric Standard Theta (θ) Table (NEW) -->
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-card-header">
        <span class="guide-tag">Trigonometry</span>
        <h3 class="guide-heading">Standard Trigonometric &theta; (Theta) Angle Value Table</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-desc">
        Exact radical and fractional values for standard angles (&theta;) in Degrees and Radians:
      </p>
      
      <!-- Responsive Trig Table -->
      <div class="trig-table-wrapper">
        <table class="trig-math-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>&theta; (Deg)</th>
              <th>&theta; (Rad)</th>
              <th>sin(&theta;)</th>
              <th>cos(&theta;)</th>
              <th>tan(&theta;)</th>
              <th>cosec(&theta;)</th>
              <th>sec(&theta;)</th>
              <th>cot(&theta;)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>0&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>30&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>&pi;/6</td>
              <td>1/2</td>
              <td>&radic;3 / 2</td>
              <td>1 / &radic;3</td>
              <td>2</td>
              <td>2 / &radic;3</td>
              <td>&radic;3</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>45&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>&pi;/4</td>
              <td>1 / &radic;2</td>
              <td>1 / &radic;2</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>&radic;2</td>
              <td>&radic;2</td>
              <td>1</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>60&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>&pi;/3</td>
              <td>&radic;3 / 2</td>
              <td>1/2</td>
              <td>&radic;3</td>
              <td>2 / &radic;3</td>
              <td>2</td>
              <td>1 / &radic;3</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>90&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>&pi;/2</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>0</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>180&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>&pi;</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>-1</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>-1</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>270&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>3&pi;/2</td>
              <td>-1</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>-1</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>0</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>360&deg;</strong></td>
              <td>2&pi;</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>&infin; (Undef)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-links">
        <span class="guide-links-title">Quick Actions:</span>
        <a href="#tool-trig" class="ctx-link">Open Interactive &theta; Calculator &rarr;</a>
        <a href="#calculator" class="ctx-link">Launch Scientific Calculator &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TrigonometricFunctions.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ctx-ext-link">Wolfram Trig Reference &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Card 1: PEMDAS & Order of Operations -->
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-card-header">
        <span class="guide-tag">Core Math</span>
        <h3 class="guide-heading">Order of Operations (PEMDAS / BODMAS)</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-desc">
        Mathematical expressions in this calculator follow standard algebraic hierarchy: <strong>Parentheses</strong>, <strong>Exponents</strong>, <strong>Multiplication & Division</strong> (left to right), and <strong>Addition & Subtraction</strong> (left to right).
      </p>
      <div class="formula-box">
        <code>Expression: 10 + 5 × 2^3 = 10 + 5 × 8 = 10 + 40 = 50</code>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <span class="guide-links-title">Contextual Links:</span>
        <a href="#calculator" class="ctx-link">Try in Main Calculator &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_operations" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ctx-ext-link" title="Wikipedia Reference">Wikipedia Order of Operations &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Card 2: Standard vs Scientific Calculator Comparison -->
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-card-header">
        <span class="guide-tag">Comparison</span>
        <h3 class="guide-heading">Standard vs. Scientific Calculator: Which to Use?</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-desc">
        <strong>Standard Mode</strong> handles daily arithmetic, shopping budgets, and invoices. <strong>Scientific Mode</strong> unlocks trigonometry (<span class="code-span">sin, cos, tan</span>), logarithms (<span class="code-span">log, ln</span>), powers (<span class="code-span">xʸ</span>), and mathematical constants (<span class="code-span">&pi;, e</span>) for physics and engineering.
      </p>
      <div class="comparison-pills">
        <span class="comp-pill">Standard: +, −, ×, ÷, %, ( )</span>
        <span class="comp-pill highlight">Scientific: Trig, Rad/Deg, Logs, Exponents</span>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="#calculator" class="ctx-link">Switch to Scientific Mode &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ctx-ext-link" title="Wolfram MathWorld">Wolfram MathWorld Reference &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Card 3: Percentage & Discount Calculations -->
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-card-header">
        <span class="guide-tag">Finance</span>
        <h3 class="guide-heading">Percentage, Discount & GST Formula Breakdown</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-desc">
        Quick reference formulas for finance calculations:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-bullet-list">
        <li><strong>Percentage of Value:</strong> <code>Amount = (Rate / 100) × Base</code></li>
        <li><strong>Discounted Price:</strong> <code>Payable = Price × (1 - Discount / 100)</code></li>
        <li><strong>Tax/GST Amount:</strong> <code>Total = Discounted Price × (1 + GST / 100)</code></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="#tool-percentage" class="ctx-link">Open Percentage Tool &rarr;</a>
        <a href="#tool-discount" class="ctx-link">Open Discount/GST Tool &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://www.cbic.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ctx-ext-link" title="Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs">Official GST Portal (CBIC) &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Card 4: BMI & Health Standards (WHO) -->
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-card-header">
        <span class="guide-tag">Health</span>
        <h3 class="guide-heading">Body Mass Index (BMI) Reference Scale</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-desc">
        Calculated as <code>BMI = weight (kg) / [height (m)]²</code> according to World Health Organization standards:
      </p>
      <div class="bmi-scale-grid">
        <div class="scale-item underweight"><span>&lt; 18.5</span><small>Underweight</small></div>
        <div class="scale-item normal"><span>18.5 - 24.9</span><small>Normal</small></div>
        <div class="scale-item overweight"><span>25.0 - 29.9</span><small>Overweight</small></div>
        <div class="scale-item obese"><span>&ge; 30.0</span><small>Obese</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="#tool-bmi" class="ctx-link">Calculate Your BMI &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/obesity-and-overweight" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ctx-ext-link" title="World Health Organization">WHO Global Guidelines &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
